"timestamp_updated": 1700542863, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.492898225784301758", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150477505", "author": {"steamid": "76561198328220721", "personaname": "Nebunedzar", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Nebunedzar/", "num_games_owned": 141, "num_reviews": 154, "playtime_forever": 43, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 43, "last_played": 1700463515, "avatar": "506634ae7dea8412734fdcd07cfb8a103dc2e1f5"}, "language": "english", "review": "Released in 2010, Alien Swarm is a free-to-play top-down shooter developed by Valve. Bringing classic co-op shooting action to PC, does Alien Swarm still hold up over a decade later? Let's find out in this review.\n\nAlien Swarm is a 4 player co-op shooter that plays from a top-down perspective, similar to classics like Gauntlet. Players team up against increasingly difficult waves of aliens across a variety of maps and environments. There's a strong emphasis on working together, managing your limited resources, and coordinating abilities to survive.\n\nThe core gameplay loop involves mowing down swarms of aliens with an arsenal of weapons like assault rifles, flamethrowers, and sentry guns. Ammo and health are scarce, so you'll need to carefully manage resources. Players choose from 4 character classes, each with unique abilities to support the team like healing, buffing damage, or deploying turrets. Missions feature objectives like destroying alien hives or protecting areas, keeping things dynamic.\n\nThe top-down visuals are fairly basic, but serviceable. Environments are destructible and aliens sport solid creature designs. Weapons all provide nice visual and sound feedback. The electronic soundtrack fits the sci-fi setting well and sound effects for the alien hordes are appropriately fierce.\n\nAlien Swarm provides good replay value through increasing difficulties, collectible weapons/upgrades, and leaderboards to compete on. The co-op focus also makes it ideal for jumping in with friends. However, the lack of enemy variety means the action can get repetitive after a while. More maps and modes would help.\n\nFor a free game, Alien Swarm delivers an exciting top-down shooter experience with loads of co-op action. The emphasis on coordination and resource management creates engaging teamwork challenges. While the gameplay can get repetitive over time, it's still a blast mowing down swarms of aliens with friends. Fans of classic twin-stick shooters should give this one a shot.", "timestamp_created": 1700464772, "timestamp_updated": 1700464772, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "150417524", "author": {"steamid": "76561198384526109", "personaname": "Green Pico", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Khainhanvn/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 27, "playtime_forever": 58, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 58, "last_played": 1528779887, "avatar": "1d3241ca5051f9084f74bc788f190967f096978c"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is the best for free to play and low end pc gamer\nWhen I Was small I used to play this game non stop \nFor the sake of nostalgia this game is a 10/10\n\nAND MORE MAPP PLS", "timestamp_created": 1700388883, "timestamp_updated": 1700388940, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": fals